**EXCERPT FROM THE MASTER SERVICES AGREEMENT**

**Section 4: Intellectual Property Rights and Compliance**

4.1 **Ownership of Intellectual Property**: All intellectual property developed by Thompson Innovations LLC ("Thompson"), located at 1234 Innovation Drive, Silicon Valley, CA, during the term of this Agreement shall be the sole property of Thompson. This includes, but is not limited to, software code, algorithms, trademarks, and patents developed for the "Project EverGreen" initiative. The parties acknowledge the involvement of Jonathan Wright, Chief Technology Officer of Thompson, and Sarah Lee, Legal Counsel for compliance matters, in overseeing the creation and protection of these assets.

4.2 **Compliance Obligations**: In accordance with the Federal Trade Commission guidelines as updated on May 15, 2023, and the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) standards, all data processed by the proprietary "DataSafe System" must adhere to specified compliance protocols. The responsibility for ensuring adherence to these protocols lies with the Compliance Department headed by Emily Chen, while the oversight of legal implications will be managed by the Litigation Team under Michael Roberts.

4.3 **Litigation Protocols**: Should any disputes arise regarding intellectual property claims, including but not limited to those involving patent infringement with GreenTech Corp., located at 5678 Greenway Blvd, Austin, TX, the parties agree to engage in mediation under the auspices of the American Arbitration Association before proceeding to litigation. All parties, including the Project Management Office led by Daniel Smith and the external legal advisors from Baker & McKenzie, shall be notified in writing at least 30 days prior to initiating any legal proceedings.

**Effective Date**: This Agreement shall take effect on October 1, 2023, and shall remain in force until terminated by either party with a written notice of 60 days.